=========================================================================
TEMPLATE A — LEATHER PRODUCT, SINGLE SIZE (full colour range)
=========================================================================
Product: Size=[One Size], Construction=[Leather]; 1 variant; CONTINUE; fixed price.
aav.swatches = [ ...leather IDs to expose..., 3 hardware IDs ]
aav.size_dimensions = {"One Size":{"cm":"45 × 45 × 45 cm","in":"17.7 × 17.7 × 17.7 in"}}
aav.configurator =
{
  "engine":"grid",
  "size_option":"Size","material_option":"Construction",
  "size_label":"Dimensions","material_label":"Construction",
  "custom_size_text":"Need a custom size?",
  "unit_map":{"One Size":"45 × 45 × 45 cm"},
  "tier_filters":{"Leather":{"category":"Leather"}},
  "pickers":[
    {"key":"leather","label":"Leather Colour","branch_by_axis":true,"property":"Leather Colour","order_swatch":true},
    {"key":"hardware","label":"Metal Finish","category":"Storage Hardware","property":"Metal Finish","order_swatch":false}
  ]
}
Notes: tier_filters with no include_names = ALL leather swatches in aav.swatches
show. To expose only 3/5 colours, list only those IDs in aav.swatches. To show
the full range, list all 10 canonical IDs (see propagation rule above).

=========================================================================
TEMPLATE B — KILIM PRODUCT, SINGLE SIZE (fixed kilim + limited trim)
=========================================================================
Product: Size=[One Size], Construction=[Kilim]; 1 variant; CONTINUE; fixed price.
aav.swatches = [ Ebony 239701065775, Chestnut 239700967471, 3 hardware IDs ]
aav.size_dimensions = {"One Size":{...}}
aav.configurator =
{
  "engine":"grid",
  "size_option":"Size","material_option":"Construction",
  "size_label":"Dimensions","material_label":"Construction",
  "custom_size_text":"Need a custom size?",
  "unit_map":{"One Size":"45 × 45 × 45 cm"},
  "material_notes":{"Kilim":"Each kilim panel is hand-cut from an assorted vintage rug, so no two pieces are alike. The exact pattern, colours and weave will differ from the photographs — that one-of-a-kind character is the essence of the piece."},
  "tier_filters":{"Kilim":{"category":"Leather","include_names":["Ebony","Chestnut"]}},
  "pickers":[
    {"key":"leather","label":"Leather Trim","branch_by_axis":true,"property":"Leather Trim","order_swatch":true},
    {"key":"hardware","label":"Metal Finish","category":"Storage Hardware","property":"Metal Finish","order_swatch":false}
  ]
}
Notes:
- Kilim is the single Construction value -> renders as a fixed label, NOT a picker.
- material_notes['Kilim'] shows the trust note under the construction label.
- tier_filters.Kilim.include_names limits trim to [Ebony, Chestnut].
- Picker label is 'Leather Trim' (vs 'Leather Colour' on leather products).
- This is the deliberate 'short by design' exception to the propagation rule.

=========================================================================
TEMPLATE C — MULTIPLE SIZES (Square / Rectangular) — kilim shown; same for leather
=========================================================================
Product: Size=[Square, Rectangular], Construction=[Kilim]; ONE VARIANT PER SIZE
(2 variants: 'Square / Kilim', 'Rectangular / Kilim'); all CONTINUE.
Prices may be equal or per-size — the engine reads price per variant.
aav.swatches = [ Ebony, Chestnut, 3 hardware IDs ]   (same as Template B)
aav.size_dimensions =
  {"Square":{"cm":"45 × 45 × 45 cm","in":"17.7 × 17.7 × 17.7 in"},
   "Rectangular":{"cm":"90 × 45 × 45 cm","in":"35.4 × 17.7 × 17.7 in"}}
aav.configurator = (as Template B) but unit_map carries BOTH size keys:
  "unit_map":{"Square":"45 × 45 × 45 cm","Rectangular":"90 × 45 × 45 cm"}
For a LEATHER multi-size product: identical, but Construction=[Leather], full
Leather Colour picker, no material_notes, tier_filters.Leather has no include_names.
REMINDER: every size value needs a matching key in BOTH size_dimensions and
unit_map, or its dimensions box is blank (see DIMENSIONS RULE above).

